Role model

This specification uses the following governance roles:

• Node steward: Maintains the node’s continuity system, coordination, dependency declarations, governance records, certification evidence, and review schedules. The node steward does not automatically control archives, authorise emergency action, or certify the node.
• Function owner: Maintains evidence and procedures for a specific critical function and coordinates practitioners, backups, apprentices, and recovery tests.
• Custodian: Preserves, documents, secures, transfers, and, where authorised, restores a specific archive, artefact, system, or custody packet. A custodian does not own the material or decide alone whether unsafe material should be executed or destroyed.
• Records steward: Maintains the integrity, accessibility, retention, correction history, and exportability of records. The records steward records decisions but does not become their sole authoriser or executor.
• Reviewer: Examines evidence, decisions, risks, or outcomes without being the sole authoriser or executor of the matter under review. Reviewers may be designated as independent, accessibility, risk, dispute, or retrospective reviewers.
• Validator: An independent reviewer or authorised quorum that makes or confirms a formal pass/fail, certification, suspension, revocation, or exceptional governance decision. A validator must not be the sole author, executor, or materially conflicted beneficiary of the decision.
• Quorum: The minimum number and composition of authorised validators required for a valid decision. Where unavailable, only explicitly permitted temporary protective action may occur.
• Test lead: Designs and coordinates a defined recovery, absence, or red-team test under approved safety controls. The test lead does not certify the result alone.
• Executor: Carries out an authorised action and records its implementation. The executor does not define the action’s authority or approve their own performance.
• Authoriser: Defines or approves the scope of an action within an established authority. The authoriser does not automatically execute or certify the action.
• Metrics steward: Compiles continuity metrics from source records. The metrics steward does not alter source records or determine certification alone.

One person may temporarily hold more than one role only under the overlap controls in Section 6. Role titles must not be used interchangeably.

