Glossary

• Node: A bounded household, group, institution, site, or federation that preserves defined critical functions and maintains its own records, dependencies, and governance.
• Critical function: A function whose loss would materially threaten life, care, essential services, knowledge, agency, safety, or future recovery options.
• Recovery test: A documented, observed exercise demonstrating whether a critical function, record, archive, role, or system can be restored after a defined failure.
• Federated partner: An independent node or organisation cooperating through recorded protocols while retaining its own governance, records, and right to pause, separate, fork, or reconnect.
• Custody packet: The records required to identify, interpret, protect, transfer, test, and, where authorised, restore significant preserved material.
• Finding: A documented condition, failure, gap, or risk identified through review, testing, incident reporting, or challenge.
• Mitigation: A corrective or compensating control intended to reduce a finding’s severity or prevent recurrence.
• Residual risk: The risk remaining after mitigation and compensating controls are implemented.
• Certification: A time-limited validator decision that the node meets the applicable requirements within a defined scope and stated conditions.
• Provisional certification: Temporary certification granted under explicit restrictions while specified evidence or corrective work remains incomplete.

