Standard checklist controls

Unless a section states a stricter requirement, every section uses the following control template:

• Checklist: The required conditions or actions.
• Pass criterion: The minimum condition for compliance.
• Fail criterion: The condition requiring corrective action or failed certification.
• Evidence standard: The records, observations, tests, or attestations needed to substantiate compliance.
• Responsible roles: The roles that prepare, execute, review, validate, and preserve the evidence.
• Review cadence: The minimum review frequency and event triggers.
• Required records: The records that must be created, retained, and made available for review.

A section passes only when its checklist is complete, its evidence meets the stated standard, and its required records are current and reviewable. A failed section must receive a severity rating and enter the corrective-action or unresolved-risk register. Section passes do not override an S3 or S4 finding elsewhere in the certification packet.

