1. Scope and safety boundary

☐ Purpose defined: The node preserves life, care, knowledge, essential functions, culture, and future options during disruption.
☐ Node type recorded: Household, clinic, workshop, farm, archive, laboratory, learning group, shelter, or federation.
☐ Prohibited actions recorded: No coercive recruitment, unauthorised access, resource seizure, political repression, forced reproduction, violence except lawful immediate protection, or classification of people as disposable.
☐ Dependency honesty confirmed: Missing capabilities are declared rather than represented as self-sufficiency.

Pass: All four items are documented and reviewable.
Fail: Any prohibited authority is claimed, or a material dependency is concealed. Such a failure is at least S3 and may be S4 if deliberate.

Evidence standard: Signed or attributable records, current dependency maps, and at least one independent review of the safety boundary.
Responsible roles: Node steward prepares the record; independent reviewer verifies it; all members may raise challenges; records steward preserves the record and challenge log.
Review cadence: At onboarding, after any material change, and at least annually.
Required records: Purpose statement, node type, prohibited-action register, dependency declaration, review decision, challenge log, and any severity or mitigation record.

