10. Minimum success metrics

Record at least:

☐ Percentage of critical functions with backups.
☐ Archive retrieval success rate.
☐ Role handoff time.
☐ Failed-function restoration time.
☐ Decisions with complete receipts.
☐ Apprentices progressing into competence.
☐ Offline and low-power availability.
☐ Accessibility of essential services.
☐ Disputes remaining inspectable after separation.
☐ Emergency actions expiring as designed.
☐ Voluntary role handoffs.
☐ Concurrent absence drill results.
☐ Recorded custody refusals with safe alternatives or witness paths.
☐ Record preservation after node separation.
☐ Capacity restored after failure.

Pass: The node demonstrates graceful degradation: life, knowledge, agency, and future options remain after tested failures.
Fail: The node measures only throughput, growth, obedience, or survival of a central authority. Metrics that conceal material failure or create coercive incentives are at least S2 and may be S3.

Evidence standard: Reproducible metric definitions, source records, calculation method, reporting period, uncertainty notes, trend comparison, and severity or mitigation records for material adverse trends.
Responsible roles: Metrics steward compiles results; function owners validate source data; independent reviewer checks interpretation and unintended incentives; records steward preserves source references; validator determines whether trends affect certification.
Review cadence: Monthly operational reporting, quarterly trend review, and annual metric-set review.
Required records: Metric dictionary, raw data references, calculation sheets, dashboard or report, validation notes, corrective actions, unresolved-risk entries, and review decisions.

